# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: entmake-duplicates-subclass-markers — validate-entity-dxf appends 100 markers the data already has
#+STATUS: OPEN
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug

* Symptom

ENTGET of an LWPOLYLINE made by RECTANG (or by any ENTMAKE whose data
already carries its markers) ends with a second copy of its subclass
markers:

: ((-1 . <Entity name: 10>) (5 . "10") (0 . "LWPOLYLINE") (100 . "AcDbEntity")
:  (100 . "AcDbPolyline") (8 . "0") (90 . 4) (70 . 1) ... (91 . 0)
:  (100 . "AcDbEntity") (100 . "AcDbPolyline"))

The vendors list each marker once, ahead of its subclass's groups.

* Repro

: (command "_.RECTANG" "0,0" "4,2") (entget (entlast))

* Cause

drawing/source/entity-families.lisp, VALIDATE-ENTITY-DXF: for a registered
family it always appends (100 . base-marker) and every family subclass
marker at the END of the data, whether or not the data already has them.
The command-probe summaries never record group 100, so the vendor
comparisons did not show it. Found 2026-10-04 while building alref S6.

* Fix

Append only the markers that are absent. For fidelity, also insert them
where the vendors put them (AcDbEntity before 8, the class marker before
the class's first group) instead of at the end.
